commit a001f21d239f06c2d31b429fd39977213222fa4c

C03: the bounded retry of a known-limit reply is plain prose, not a JSON-grammar object (UI1663)

UI1659 and UI1661 measured «Andá al canal general en Discord.» ending in a clarification: the first draft hit the double-inability rule («no puedo … ni …») and the bounded retry, constrained to a JSON object by grammar, spent its 96 tokens on whitespace and returned empty content (finish_reason length). Reproduced offline with the product runtime (chatprobe.py). For an unsupported-contract failure the retry drops response_format: the limit contract validates the sentence itself, and the plain retry yields «No puedo acceder al canal general en Discord tal como fue pedido.».

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


